Bug: `Context.Scheme()` is documented as "Scheme returns the HTTP protocol scheme, `http` or `https`", but it currently returns whatever value the X-Forwarded-Proto / X-Forwarded-Protocol / X-Url-Scheme request headers contain, even when the value is not a valid HTTP scheme (e.g. `ftp`). Expected: invalid values are ignored and the next fallback header is consulted; if no valid value is found the default `http` is returned.

Fix: replace the body of `func (c *context) Scheme() string` (currently around line 252) with exactly:

```go
func (c *context) Scheme() string {
	// Can't use `r.Request.URL.Scheme`
	// See: https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/golang-nuts/pMUkBlQBDF0
	if c.IsTLS() {
		return "https"
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProto); scheme == "http" || scheme == "https" {
		return scheme
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProtocol); scheme == "http" || scheme == "https" {
		return scheme
	}
	if ssl := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedSsl); ssl == "on" {
		return "https"
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXUrlScheme); scheme == "http" || scheme == "https" {
		return scheme
	}
	return "http"
}
```

